{
  "query": "YubiKey SSH \"agent refused operation\" PKCS11 OpenSC fix ssh-agent",
  "results": [
    {
      "title": "YubiKey SSH \"agent refused operation\" PKCS11 OpenSC fix ssh-agent",
      "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/yubikey/comments/123456/yubikey_ssh_agent_refused_operation_pkcs11/",
      "snippet": "I'm trying to use my YubiKey 5C NFC with SSH on macOS. I've followed various guides, installed OpenSC, and configured ssh-agent to use the PKCS11 module. However, when I try to `ssh-add -s /usr/local/lib/opensc-pkcs11.so`, I get \"agent refused operation\". I've tried restarting ssh-agent, rebooting, and even reinstalling OpenSC. Any ideas?"
    },
    {
      "title": "Troubleshooting YubiKey SSH with OpenSC and PKCS11",
      "url": "https://developers.yubico.com/yubikey-manager/SSH_Troubleshooting.html",
      "snippet": "This guide covers common issues when using a YubiKey for SSH authentication with OpenSC and PKCS11. The \"agent refused operation\" error often indicates a problem with the `ssh-agent` configuration, permissions, or the YubiKey itself. Ensure `ssh-agent` is running and properly configured to load the PKCS11 module. Check `~/.ssh/config` for any conflicting settings. Sometimes, restarting `ssh-agent` or even the system can resolve transient issues. Verify that the YubiKey is correctly inserted and recognized by the system using `ykman list`."
    },
    {
      "title": "Using YubiKey for SSH authentication on Linux - DigitalOcean",
      "url": "https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-use-yubikey-for-ssh-authentication-on-linux",
      "snippet": "This tutorial walks through setting up a YubiKey for SSH authentication on a Linux system. It covers installing necessary tools like `opensc` and `yubikey-manager`, generating SSH keys on the YubiKey, and configuring `ssh-agent` to use the PKCS11 module. If you encounter \"agent refused operation\", double-check the path to your PKCS11 module and ensure `ssh-agent` has the correct permissions to access it. Also, verify that your YubiKey is properly initialized and has an SSH key stored on it."
    },
    {
      "title": "Fixing 'agent refused operation' with YubiKey and SSH on Ubuntu",
      "url": "https://askubuntu.com/questions/1234567/fixing-agent-refused-operation-with-yubikey-and-ssh-on-ubuntu",
      "snippet": "I'm having trouble getting my YubiKey to work with SSH on Ubuntu 20.04. When I try to add the PKCS11 module to `ssh-agent`, I get \"agent refused operation\". I've tried various solutions, including ensuring `ssh-agent` is running, checking permissions on `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/opensc-pkcs11.so`, and restarting the agent. One user suggested checking the `SSH_AUTH_SOCK` environment variable. Another suggested trying `ssh-add -L` to see if any keys are already loaded."
    },
    {
      "title": "YubiKey SSH setup guide with OpenSC and PKCS11 - GitHub Gist",
      "url": "https://gist.github.com/someuser/abcdef1234567890",
      "snippet": "A comprehensive guide to setting up YubiKey for SSH with OpenSC and PKCS11. Includes steps for installing dependencies, configuring `ssh-agent`, and troubleshooting common errors. If you get \"agent refused operation\", ensure your `~/.gnupg/scdaemon.conf` is correctly configured, and that `ssh-agent` is not conflicting with `gpg-agent`. Sometimes, explicitly setting `SSH_AUTH_SOCK` can help. Also, make sure your YubiKey firmware is up to date."
    }
  ]
}

